    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days(start, n, holidays=())` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`. It validates inputs first: `start` must be a `date` and not a `datetime`, `n` must be an `int` (with `bool` and `float` rejected), and every holiday must be a `date` and not a `datetime`. Holidays are collected into a set, so any iterable works, including generators. For `n > 0` and `n < 0` it steps one calendar day at a time in that direction and counts business days, never counting `start`. For `n == 0` it returns `start` if that is a business day, otherwise the next one. I wrote `tests/test_solution.py` with 25 tests covering forward and backward moves, weekend starts, the zero case, holidays (including weekend holidays, consecutive holidays and generator input) and the `TypeError` cases. Running `python -m pytest -q tests` gives 25 passed. I did not add or change anything else, and no packages were installed.",
